      "object_id": "mathia_interpretation_5129d20135a782a4a2330b8f397ba6111024a790927ee97fb8665e83d6550258",
      "object_role": "interpretation",
      "proposed_content": "The same critical-line anchors do not determine a unique off-line geometry; the multiplier choice controls how phase propagates. In the average problem, functional-equation duality contributes a coherent term that is invisible at σ=1/2 only because it then has constant size.",
