    {
      "object_id": "mathia_synthesis_206aecc817c82c2d58bdabf1fb42933f89876b63d80f7fdf27adda2385824a32",
      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "The source uses phase-normalized functional-equation multipliers as genuinely different geometric representations: Lambda-real and Phi-real contours share Gram-point anchors on the critical line, but Lambda-real contours are asymptotically horizontal and carry a monotone signed multiplier whose reflected-zero derivative comparison has no stated Phi analogue, whereas Phi-real contours have a logarithmically small negative slope.",
