    {
      "object_id": "mathia_synthesis_787480b2ced335c6dc05d8976b01d461b13fc1f01b7baecff862bdeb89ceaaa0",
      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "At Gram ordinates the Lambda phase makes chi=1/Lambda asymptotically real, so the approximate functional equation separates a coherent dual contribution, (g_n/2pi)^(1/2-sigma), from two oscillatory Dirichlet families. Curvature of the inverse Gram map supplies fixed-frequency cancellation, and reversing/partially summing the double sums turns that cancellation into the uniform corrected-mean theorem after balancing the absolute-convergence and dual-sum regimes.",
